### Feature Difficulty Rankings (Easiest → Hardest)

| # | Feature | Difficulty | Why |
|---|---------|-----------|-----|
| 1 | **Favicons on tabs** | Trivial | WebView2 has `CoreWebView2.FaviconUri` + `FaviconChanged` event. Just add the URL to your JSON payload and render an `<img>` in the HTML tab strip. Fallback to `https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain={host}` if empty. |
| 2 | **Custom app icon** | Trivial | One-line `.csproj` change or project property. If it "didn't work," Windows is caching the old icon in Explorer/Taskbar. |
| 3 | **Audio indicator** | Easy | WebView2 has `CoreWebView2.IsMuted` and `IsDocumentPlayingAudioChanged` event. Add a boolean to the tab payload, show a small speaker wave icon in HTML when true. |
| 4 | **Download progress bar** | Easy-Med | WebView2 has `CoreWebView2.DownloadStarting` event. Track active downloads in a list, pass progress to the chrome UI. Requires a small C# download manager class. |
| 5 | **Force Dark Mode** | Easy-Med | WebView2 has `CoreWebView2.Profile.PreferredColorScheme = Dark`. Also `SetVirtualHostNameToFolderMapping` with a CSS injector, or use the built-in WebView2 auto-dark feature. Mostly a settings toggle. |
| 6 | **Hibernated tabs** | Medium | Requires unloading the WebView2 (navigate to `about:blank` or dispose the control) while keeping the tab metadata (URL, title, favicon) in memory. On click, recreate the WebView2 and re-navigate. Tricky: restoring scroll position and form state later. |
| 7 | **Screenshot button** | Medium | WebView2 has `CoreWebView2.CapturePreviewAsync` (PNG stream) or `ShowPrintUI`. Save the stream to a file. Requires a file dialog and async handling. |
| 8 | **Quick Actions / Command Palette** | Medium-Hard | Needs a new HTML overlay (`Ctrl+K`), a fuzzy search index across tabs/history/bookmarks, and a message bridge back to C#. The UI is easy; building the searchable index and wiring all commands is the work. |
| 9 | **Reader Mode** | Hard | No native WebView2 API for this. You must inject a JavaScript readability library (like Mozilla's Readability.js) into the page, parse the DOM, extract article content, then render it in a clean internal page. Requires JS injection + DOM parsing + a custom reader template. |
| 10 | **Picture-in-Picture** | Hard | WebView2 doesn't expose PiP directly. You'd need to spawn a **second tiny borderless WinForms window** with its own WebView2, sync the video element from the main page via JS interop, and keep it always-on-top. Very finicky. |
| 11 | **QR Code generator** | Medium | Generate a QR bitmap in C# (using a NuGet like `QRCoder` — 1 line of code), then pass the image bytes as base64 to the chrome UI to display in a popup. The hard part is the popup UI, not the QR generation. |

