### How to Set the App Icon (The Right Way)

If it didn't work, you probably set `this.Icon` on the form but not the **application icon**. Windows Explorer and the Taskbar show the **application icon**, not the form icon.

**Method 1: `.csproj` file (Recommended — this is what Explorer sees)**

Open `Yalb.Maeger.csproj` and add:

```xml
<PropertyGroup>
  <ApplicationIcon>Assets\yalb-icon.ico</ApplicationIcon>
</PropertyGroup>

<ItemGroup>
  <Content Include="Assets\yalb-icon.ico" />
</ItemGroup>
```

Then rebuild. The `.ico` file must be a real multi-resolution icon (16×16, 32×32, 48×48, 256×256). A single PNG renamed to `.ico` will fail silently in some places.

**Method 2: Form icon (Taskbar thumbnail)**

In `BrowserForm.cs` constructor or `Load`:

```csharp
this.Icon = new Icon("Assets\\yalb-icon.ico");
```

**If it still doesn't update:** Windows caches application icons aggressively.
- Right-click the `.exe` → Properties → Change Icon → pick the `.ico` again
- Or delete `%LocalAppData%\IconCache.db` and restart Explorer

