### How to Get Favicons on Tabs

**Step 1: Listen in C#**

In your `WebView2` initialization for each tab's content view:

```csharp
contentWebView.CoreWebView2.FaviconChanged += (s, e) =>
{
    var faviconUrl = contentWebView.CoreWebView2.FaviconUri;
    // Add faviconUrl to your tab model
    UpdateChromeUIAsync(); // re-serialize tabs with favicon
};
```

**Step 2: Add to your JSON payload**

In `UpdateChromeUIAsync()`, include a `favicon` field per tab:

```json
{
  "tabs": [
    { "id": "tab-1", "title": "GitHub", "url": "...", "favicon": "https://github.com/favicon.ico", "active": true }
  ]
}
```

**Step 3: Render in `chrome-ui/index.html`**

In your tab rendering JS:

```javascript
function renderTab(tab) {
  const img = tab.favicon 
    ? `<img src="${tab.favicon}" class="tab-favicon" onerror="this.src='https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=${new URL(tab.url).host}'">`
    : `<span class="tab-favicon-placeholder"></span>`;
  
  return `<div class="tab" data-id="${tab.id}">
    ${img}
    <span class="tab-title">${tab.title}</span>
    <span class="tab-close">×</span>
  </div>`;
}
```

**Fallback rule:** If `favicon` is empty or the image fails to load (`onerror`), use Goo gle's public favicon service: `https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=github.com`. This catches 99% of sites.